<title>USA: GM shares rise after strike settlement.</title>
<headline>GM shares rise after strike settlement.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp shares were up 1-5/8 to 58-1/2 late Monday afternoon after the car maker struck a deal over the weekend to end a transmission plant strike and avert a broad shutdown of its North American operations.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a perception that we're getting to the end of the labor troubles,&quot; said J.P. Morgan auto analyst David Bradley. &quot;We could be entering a period of clean earnings without the labor unrest.&quot;</p>
</text>
